t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). By contrast, the National Women's Soccer League maintains a detailed policy that mandates game modifications or postponements when the air quality index reaches specific thresholds, such as 101 or 200 [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesn't have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). Neither FIFA nor New York City Department of Health officials immediately responded to Grist's request for comment [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesn't have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/).ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;gIWQg2JOkWcZ8vRH956FiC5wpAuSZzVqZx8xFcxiKiEƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkwreplace_exact_body_textƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;k66TPKwMRYmkV9nbPY8yE6ePWIgYUDDeE0ercMmP7FYƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;gdgk3pWZleel0OjdJruOvYlfEwWDcFdgtm1mIXNlFNoƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarky9The smoke also poses particular risks to children, older individuals, and those with respiratory conditions such as asthma [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesn't have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/).ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;AlYFDxg5ycAPCGwjQZOLTKXslRPaHLtFhqTeEa0EKkcƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkypVulnerable groups, including children, older individuals, and those with pre-existing conditions like asthma, also face increased dangers from the current air quality conditions [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesn't have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/).ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;uify1DQpHd7viK6YsuzQZwhS74FuyT4d-42171yWby4ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkwreplace_exact_body_textƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;TDr_pXU35rnMd4vaJYva75SD9L9tsCtWLBDm1K8oyoEƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;ocip7xDz3GM1QYeDrFl5nTZSowP2rKxWwLnOsq_DG48ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarky‡As of Friday morning, conditions near the stadium remained unhealthy, with forecasters expecting improvement to moderate by Sunday's kickoff but cautioning that smoke patterns remain subject to change [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesn't have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/).ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;DB0Lhg0I4IpodJEkKYOCL1U8sO-iCmvxkm40zqfhLzsƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarky³Forecasters continue to track smoke patterns, with officials noting that conditions near the stadium remained in the unhealthy range as of Friday morning [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesn't have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). While New York City has experienced hazy, orange skies throughout the week, the specific quality of the air on Sunday will depend on shifting wind patterns [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesn't have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/).ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;P5y4lVsGMaIE9kTf9pboFNwgIvDLzsm2Yf4brui-qbAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkwreplace_exact_body_textƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;SDorTpLCovpnpaitDVkl6muasTjkRcNPDz4mjG_NO4Mƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;Js29n6XFuOO7OhrAvQq9rs79dj4qrZ6MDqwDTE_psUEƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx!## FIFA Has No Air Quality Policyƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;SHdSRobSRUXbU3-ETJOWWR0s1wNcA4thqU4vJKzSUgcƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx&## A Gap in Institutional Preparednessƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;EmXx9agpowOlbLQ9vIfdVFxxP91DBZ_EFo7QwE_APIcƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkwreplace_exact_body_textƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;X-NMmfAcO0zKfc_mCMCFfFPzUN0vAud_oXVZKBpmI3Iƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;ekdqIX5og1IqYBz9gjCEAgywRPo-I0H1c-TJh7Hq78sƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxrepair_editorial_surfacesƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;BRshZgLYovi5A--ZofQv6EPEeWqNbg0Khk-5pZQnpr4ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarklwriter-modelƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;7dwWh_K_5SMfikiFxWMBE-kJHETWk0czph4vS4Fy4bEƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkyPIPELINE DIAGNOSIS. This manuscript is a single-source aggregation of Grist's July 17, 2026 investigation into FIFA's wildfire smoke preparedness gap. The assignment is sound, the source is relevant, and all material factual claims trace to the witnessed research packet. The failure layer is writer-model: the draft generated pervasively repetitive paragraphs (eleven near-duplicate proximity warnings across all four body sections), omitted FIFA's only on-record climate statement despite its clear presence in the source, and produced malformed editorial surfaces.

SOURCE AND ATTRIBUTION AUDIT. Every factual claim in the body is supported by the witnessed Grist source: Canadian wildfire smoke blanketing the Midwest and East Coast; AQI climbing to unhealthy and very unhealthy levels Thursday; New York state alerts; the open-air stadium; FIFA's apparent absence of an air quality policy; the NWSL thresholds at AQI 101 and 200; Dr. Courtney Howard's credentials and quote to the Associated Press (correctly attributed to AP, not to this outlet); Watanabe's institutional affiliation and closing quote; and the proper attribution of unanswered media inquiries to Grist's request rather than to this outlet. Inline hyperlink attribution is present and consistent throughout. The headline and lede are faithful to the source thesis. No claim materially exceeds what the source can sustain. The editorial risk flag "primary-source-unproven" is duly noted: Grist is an intermediary, not a primary agency record, but the manuscript's consistent attribution via inline hyperlink makes that provenance transparent.

NEAR-DUPLICATE PROXIMITY â€” ALL FOUR PARAGRAPHS. The deterministic copy-edit gate flagged eleven near-duplicate sentence pairs, distributed across every body section. In paragraph 1, three sentences cluster overlapping information about the World Cup location, Canadian smoke, and AQI into adjacent sentences that share multiple short phrases, producing three flagged pairs from a single three-sentence paragraph. In paragraph 2, the FIFA-no-policy sentence, the NWSL-contrast sentence, and the no-response sentence are individually accurate but together generate three flagged pairs from shared topical phrasing. In paragraph 3, the vulnerable-populations sentence shares topical phrasing with the Dr. Howard athlete quote immediately above it. In paragraph 4, "Forecasters continue to track smoke patterns" and "While New York City has experienced hazy, orange skies" cover overlapping territory and generate three flagged pairs with each other and with the Watanabe closing quote. All four paragraph-level problems are compression artifacts from the writer model and are correctable by bounded replace_exact_body_text operations without altering any factual content.

FAIRNESS GAP â€” MATERIAL. The source article contains FIFA's only substantive on-record public statement: "In a previous statement to Grist, FIFA detailed extensive protocols related to extreme heat, including mandatory water breaks for players, but didn't mention air quality. 'Climate-related risks,' the organization wrote last month, 'are assessed as part of overall tournament planning and managed in close coordination with host cities, stadium authorities, and national agencies.'" The manuscript omits this entirely. Under ordinary newsroom fairness standards, when a manuscript criticizes an institution for lacking a policy, that institution's on-record words must appear â€” especially when those words are in the admitted source and were available to the writer. The no-response disclosure that appears in paragraph 2 refers to a separate, current inquiry by Grist, not to this prior statement, so it does not substitute. The repair inserts the prior statement into the institutional gap section between the NWSL comparison and the no-response disclosure.

WATANABE QUOTE CONTEXT â€” MINOR, NOT SEPARATELY REQUIRED. The manuscript quotes Watanabe's "wakeup call" sentence in isolation. His immediately preceding statement â€” "FIFA seems unprepared for these wildfires. At the same time, it looks like the worst of the pollution will dissipate before the World Cup Final, so FIFA will dodge a bullet and likely push forward with the match" â€” establishes that his assessment is conditional rather than purely alarmed. The solo quote is not inaccurate but is slightly selective in presentation. Not elevated to a separate required repair given the bounded scope of existing corrections, but the writer should be aware.

EDITORIAL SURFACES. The description field reads "Neither FIFA nor New York City Department of Health officials immediately responded to Grist's request for comment" â€” a verbatim sentence lifted from the article body, not a meta-description. The summary juxtaposes two thematically disconnected sentences (lede geography and NWSL threshold data) without editorial coherence. Both surfaces must be regenerated from the admitted body via repair_editorial_surfaces.

DEMAND-LENS H2. The deterministic gate warned that no H2 naturally signals the demand lens. "A Gap in Institutional Preparedness" is abstract; readers searching "wildfire smoke threatens cup final fifa doesn plan" want a direct answer to whether there is a plan. "FIFA Has No Air Quality Policy" answers the demand query directly and is supported by the admitted body.

